From: damnbitimcrit <333091414+damnbitimcrit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Halo 3] Fix per-frame code that assumed 30 frames per second

With the frame rate unlocked the main loop body runs once per drawn frame
instead of once per 30 Hz tick. While unlocked:

- Shader and effect "time" inputs, computed from the tick counter in four
  render input providers, get the fraction of a tick since the last one
  added, so animated shaders and effect functions move smoothly.
- The two HUD fades that stepped a fixed 1/15 per frame scale the step by
  frame time.
- The UI and HUD millisecond clocks carry the truncated fraction of each
  frame's time to the next frame instead of losing it.
- Debris (muffins) keeps the overshoot when it takes its 1/30 s step
  instead of resetting the accumulator.
- The wind random walk steps once per tick instead of once per drawn frame,
  its time input is smooth, and the per-call gust increment scales with
  frame time.
- Sound needs nothing: its fades and slews step by the sound clock's own
  elapsed time.
---
